      "criterion": "WHEN processing a session stream, THE SYSTEM SHALL execute the 19 EntryAccumulator-based accumulators in a single linear pass over the parsed turns in O(N) time. Heap allocation in the inner loop SHALL be minimized and reviewed statically per accumulator, not verified via a custom global allocator: this workspace sets unsafe_code = \"forbid\" (Cargo.toml), and implementing Rust's GlobalAlloc trait requires an unsafe impl block, making a runtime allocation-counting harness structurally impossible to build here. token_usage and hook_activity are exempt by design: both are RawMessageAccumulators operating on raw pre-parse JSON messages, invoked independently of AnalyticsEngine::process_transcript, not inside its per-turn loop. otel_correlation is exempt by design: it reads the whole CanonicalTranscript once, post-loop, rather than per-turn.",
      "is_error_case": false,
      "judgment_call": false,
      "reasoning": "Originally worded as requiring an empirically-measured zero-heap-allocation guarantee. A static audit (2026-08-20, during TASK-ANALYSIS-003) found 6 apparent violations. On closer engineering review, these split into two genuinely different categories: (1) AVOIDABLE, now fixed: circuit_breaker.rs called format!(\"parent->{agent_type}\") on every SubagentSpawn call, allocating a throwaway String before wrapping it in CompactString -- replaced with direct construction via CompactString::const_new(\"parent->\") + std::fmt::Write, which uses CompactString's own inline buffer when the result fits (compact_str 0.8 supports fmt::Write directly). pr_link.rs's unconditional per-turn BTreeMap::collect() was similarly found and fixed earlier in the same pass. (2) INHERENT, not a defect: artifacts.rs, tool_inventory.rs, fuzzy_tools.rs, attribution.rs, and trajectory_dag.rs each clone CompactString data into an owned BTreeMap/BTreeSet/Vec that must outlive the borrowed per-turn CanonicalTurn data and persist until finalize() -- this is the necessary cost of building any deduplicated or aggregated accumulator output at all, not wasted work. Eliminating these would require a fundamentally different architecture (e.g. arena-based string interning), which is a substantially larger investment than this criterion contemplated and is not undertaken here."
